    {
      "node_id": "kg_doc_8",
      "node_type": "kg",
      "content": "Barking Dogs Never Bite (Korean: 플란다스의 개 , also known as \"A Higher Animal\" and \"Dog of Flanders\") is a 2000 South Korean dark comedy-drama film. The film's original Korean title is a satirical take on \"A Dog of Flanders\", a European pet story that is very popular in parts of East Asia. It is also the directorial debut of Bong Joon-ho, who would later go on to direct \"Memories of Murder\" in 2003, \"The Host\" in 2006, and \"Snowpiercer\" in 2013.",
      "depth": 0,
      "parent_id": null,
      "value": 0.9999999909916727,
      "temperature": 0.9999999909916727,
      "expanded": false,
      "visit_count": 0,
